  3Challenges to a circuit court’s subject-matter jurisdiction under sovereign immunity  principles are often raised in the circuit court proceeding by filing a motion pursuant to  section 2-619(a)(1) of the Code of Civil Procedure (735 ILCS 5/2-619(a)(1) (West 2020)).  Walker v. Chasteen, 2025 IL 130288, ¶ 16 (“When a defendant claims that sovereign  immunity divests the circuit court of jurisdiction, section 2-619(a)(1) prescribes a motion  to dismiss that alleges ‘the court does not have jurisdiction of the subject matter of the  action, provided the defect cannot be removed by a transfer of the case to a court having  jurisdiction.’ ” (quoting 735 ILCS 5/2-619(a)(1) (West 2020))).  
    
